The “Win-Win: Gender Equality means Good Business” an partnership Programme between UN Women, the International Labour Organization (ILO) and the European Union (EU), implemented through the EU Service for Foreign Policy Instruments (FPI), between January 2018 and August 2021 . 

The Programme underpins on the recognition of women as beneficiaries and partners of sustainable growth, while aiming at increasing the commitment of private and public companies to gender equality and women´s empowerment and strengthening the companies’ capacities to implement these commitments. Targeting women-led enterprises and networks, Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs), multi-national companies, employers’ organizations and relevant stakeholders in Europe and six selected Latin American and Caribbean countries (Argentina, Brazil, Chile, Costa Rica, Jamaica, and Uruguay), the key, interlinked objectives to achieve the impact are:
1.	Support women-led business in Europe and LAC, including European companies located in LAC, to increase cooperation and expand opportunities;
2.	Develop and adopt a sustainable model of gender sensitive private sector engagement to support Sustainable Development Goals´ (SGDs) achievement, in order to promote gender equal business to encourage wider adherence, implementation and reporting on the Women’s Empowerment Principles (WEPs);
3.	Increase bi-regional women led innovation and business ventures through the establishment of an investment facility as a sustainable financing model that attracts additional and longer-term private sector investments for gender equality and the achievement of SDGs.

